  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q39-46-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Prove the following identities.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p31-q39-46-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\sin 2\\theta(1-\\cos\\theta)}{\\cos\\theta(1-\\cos 2\\theta)}=\\tan\\dfrac{\\theta}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\mathrm{LHS}=\\dfrac{1-\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}=\\tan\\dfrac{\\theta}{2}=\\mathrm{RHS}$.\n\nUse double-angle substitutions, then the half-angle identity.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta(1-\\cos\\theta)}{2\\cos\\theta\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{1-\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{2\\sin^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}}{2\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\tan\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\mathrm{RHS}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q39-46-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta-\\sin\\theta}=\\sec 2\\theta+\\tan 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\mathrm{LHS}=\\dfrac{1+\\sin 2\\theta}{\\cos 2\\theta}=\\sec 2\\theta+\\tan 2\\theta=\\mathrm{RHS}$.\n\nMultiply numerator and denominator by $\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{(\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta)^2}{(\\cos\\theta-\\sin\\theta)(\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta)}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{\\cos^2\\theta+2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{1+\\sin 2\\theta}{\\cos 2\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\sec 2\\theta+\\tan 2\\theta\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\mathrm{RHS}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q39-46-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}-\\theta\\right)+\\tan\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}+\\theta\\right)=2\\sec 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\mathrm{LHS}=\\dfrac{2(1+\\tan^2\\theta)}{1-\\tan^2\\theta}=\\dfrac{2}{\\cos 2\\theta}=2\\sec 2\\theta=\\mathrm{RHS}$.\n\nExpand both tangents and combine the fractions.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{1-\\tan\\theta}{1+\\tan\\theta}+\\frac{1+\\tan\\theta}{1-\\tan\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{(1-\\tan\\theta)^2+(1+\\tan\\theta)^2}{1-\\tan^2\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{2(1+\\tan^2\\theta)}{1-\\tan^2\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{2(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)}{\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=2\\sec 2\\theta\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\mathrm{RHS}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q39-46-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\sin 2\\theta\\cos\\theta}{(1+\\cos 2\\theta)(1+\\cos\\theta)}=\\tan\\dfrac{\\theta}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\mathrm{LHS}=\\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{1+\\cos\\theta}=\\tan\\dfrac{\\theta}{2}=\\mathrm{RHS}$.\n\nUse $1+\\cos 2\\theta=2\\cos^2\\theta$, then the taught half-angle identity.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{2\\sin\\theta\\cos^2\\theta}{2\\cos^2\\theta(1+\\cos\\theta)}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{1+\\cos\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{2\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}}{2\\cos^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\tan\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\mathrm{RHS}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q39-46-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$(1+\\tan\\theta)^2-\\sec^2\\theta=\\sin 2\\theta\\sec^2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Both sides equal $2\\tan\\theta$.\n\nExpand the square and use $\\sec^2\\theta=1+\\tan^2\\theta$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=1+2\\tan\\theta+\\tan^2\\theta-(1+\\tan^2\\theta)\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=2\\tan\\theta.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{RHS}&=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\cdot\\frac{1}{\\cos^2\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{RHS}&=2\\tan\\theta\\\\\\mathrm{RHS}&=\\mathrm{LHS}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q39-46-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2\\cos\\theta+1+\\cos 2\\theta}{2\\cos\\theta-1-\\cos 2\\theta}=\\left(\\dfrac{1+\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\\right)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\mathrm{LHS}=\\dfrac{1+\\cos\\theta}{1-\\cos\\theta}=\\left(\\dfrac{1+\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\\right)^2=\\mathrm{RHS}$.\n\nSubstitute $\\cos 2\\theta=2\\cos^2\\theta-1$, factor, and use half-angle identities.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{2\\cos\\theta+2\\cos^2\\theta}{2\\cos\\theta-2\\cos^2\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{2\\cos\\theta(1+\\cos\\theta)}{2\\cos\\theta(1-\\cos\\theta)}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{1+\\cos\\theta}{1-\\cos\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{2\\cos^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}}{2\\sin^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\left(\\frac{2\\cos^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}}{2\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}}\\right)^2\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\left(\\frac{1+\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\\right)^2\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\mathrm{RHS}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q39-46-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\sin 4\\theta(1-\\cos 2\\theta)}{\\cos 2\\theta(1-\\cos 4\\theta)}=\\tan\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\mathrm{LHS}=\\dfrac{2\\sin^2\\theta}{\\sin 2\\theta}=\\tan\\theta=\\mathrm{RHS}$.\n\nApply the double-angle identities at $\\theta$ and $2\\theta$, then cancel factors.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{(2\\sin 2\\theta\\cos 2\\theta)(2\\sin^2\\theta)}{\\cos 2\\theta(2\\sin^2 2\\theta)}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{2\\sin^2\\theta}{\\sin 2\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{2\\sin^2\\theta}{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\tan\\theta\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\mathrm{RHS}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q39-46-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\sin 2\\alpha\\sin 2\\beta}{\\cos 2\\alpha+\\cos 2\\beta}=\\dfrac{2\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta}{1-\\tan^2\\alpha\\tan^2\\beta}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\mathrm{LHS}=\\dfrac{2\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta}{1-\\tan^2\\alpha\\tan^2\\beta}=\\mathrm{RHS}$.\n\nExpand both sine factors, choose complementary cosine expansions, and divide numerator and denominator by $\\cos^2\\alpha\\cos^2\\beta$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{4\\sin\\alpha\\cos\\alpha\\sin\\beta\\cos\\beta}{(2\\cos^2\\alpha-1)+(1-2\\sin^2\\beta)}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{4\\sin\\alpha\\cos\\alpha\\sin\\beta\\cos\\beta}{2(\\cos^2\\alpha-\\sin^2\\beta)}.\\end{align*}$$\nDivide numerator and denominator by $\\cos^2\\alpha\\cos^2\\beta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{4\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta}{2(\\sec^2\\beta-\\tan^2\\beta\\sec^2\\alpha)}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{2\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta}{(1+\\tan^2\\beta)-\\tan^2\\beta(1+\\tan^2\\alpha)}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{2\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta}{1-\\tan^2\\alpha\\tan^2\\beta}\\\\\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\mathrm{RHS}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      }
    ]
  },
